5. STEP 2 -- PUTTING A REAL SCRIPT ON THE DEVICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two routes were available and neither is a STANDING-ORDERS §4 item (triage established
both): stage the file in the box's `/tftproot` (mode 1777, `tftpd-hpa` active) and pull it
with `copy tftp://10.38.22.33/<f>.scp flash:/<f>.scp`, or write it on the DUT through
`start-shell`. The second was used, because it needs nothing on the testbox at all and
`tools/tb` has no action that writes outside `/tmp/<scratch>/`.

Said plainly: this case used tools/awshell.py, a `start-shell` root shell ON THE DUT, to
create two files under /flash and to read them back. `start-shell` is logged on the device
(`IMISH[...]: [manager@ttyS0]start-shell`), so the session is auditable. Nothing else was
written in that shell, and both files are deleted in STEP 6 with `dir flash:` as proof.

  [root@awplus ~]# printf 'enable\nconfigure terminal\ninterface port1.0.20\ndescription CKT33403-ACTIVATE-RAN\nend\n' > /flash/ckt3a.scp
  [root@awplus ~]# printf 'enable\nconfigure terminal\ninterface port1.0.21\ndescription CKT33403-TRIGGER-RAN\nend\n' > /flash/ckt3b.scp
  [root@awplus ~]# ls -l /flash/ckt3a.scp /flash/ckt3b.scp
  -rw-r-----    1 root     wheel           85 Oct 22 01:07 /flash/ckt3a.scp
  -rw-r-----    1 root     wheel           84 Oct 22 01:07 /flash/ckt3b.scp
  [root@awplus ~]# cat /flash/ckt3a.scp
  enable
  configure terminal
  interface port1.0.20
  description CKT33403-ACTIVATE-RAN
  end
  [root@awplus ~]# cat /flash/ckt3b.scp
  enable
  configure terminal
  interface port1.0.21
  description CKT33403-TRIGGER-RAN
  end

  The artefact each script leaves is an INTERFACE DESCRIPTION with a unique string. A
  description is a good artefact for this case: it is visible in `show running-config`,
  it is saved by `write` so persistence can be tested, it has no effect on forwarding, and
  nothing else on the device would ever produce that text.

  Both files appear from the CLI too:
  awplus# dir flash:
        84 -rw- Oct 22 2026 01:07:20  ckt3b.scp
        85 -rw- Oct 22 2026 01:07:19  ckt3a.scp
  (method note: `dir flash: | include scp` is REJECTED -- "% Invalid input detected at
   '^' marker." `dir` does not take a pipe filter on this platform.)

